mmands precede Fields and own contextual input/output contracts; procedures select capabilities and preserve their guards and continuations. The skill's declared model drives shared validation while common runtime context has focused homes.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Shared Validation\n\n- **Declared models.**\n  Per-skill declarations select section layout, heading steps, preambles, command specifications, role tags and Run/Apply/Follow routing.\n- **Literal boundaries.**\n  One lexical reader distinguishes executable invocations from specimens and validates their linked arguments without treating payload text as procedure structure.\n\n### Command Contracts\n\n- **Contextual specifications.**\n  Commands own an imperative action/result preamble, one linked HTML invocation and meaningful usage conditions; callers retain selections and result handling.\n- **Readable arguments.**\n  Encoded shell continuations preserve literal syntax; quoting follows value type, and Fields carry same-line inline examples while structural templates retain fences.\n\n### Instruction Ownership\n\n- **Focused context.**\n  Rules, Conventions and Configuration have dedicated homes; in-text links select context, and Rules defines input, output and callable link roles once.\n- **Data and procedures.**\n  Fields describe values and valid-state constraints; single-use rules accompany their caller, shared policy has one Guidance home, and shared operations retain meaningful processing.\n- **Preserved execution.**\n  Explicit empty/optional values, output paths, formatter evidence, reservation dates, repeated base revisions and delivery/closure gates retain their consuming behavior.\n\n### Consumer Validation\n\n- **Actual contracts.**\n  Fixtures execute documented invocations against real local readers and temporary repositories, covering concrete result shapes and failure evidence.\n- **Current catalogue.**\n  Test documentation and its reader describe current modules, root documents and counts, with the current target incorporated on the integration branch.\n\n## References\n\n- **R1.** [Skill Models](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1640) — declared-model support and specimen coverage.\n- **R2.** [Common Files](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1642) — Rules, Conventions and Configuration.\n- **R3.** [Mode Procedures](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1643) — mode conversion and consumer readers.\n- **R4.** [Protocol Procedures](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1644) — protocol conversion and continuation preservation.\n- **R5.** [Issue and Body Artifacts](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1646) — body contracts and artifact conversion.\n- **R6.** [Board and Planning Artifacts](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1651) — board, queue, planning and review contracts.\n- **R7.** [Delivery Artifacts](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1647) — delivery, branch and PR contracts.\n- **R8.** [Style Activation](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1652) — installed guidelines and model declarations.\n- **R9.** [Agent Review](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-06-1641-integration-review/agent-review.json) — exact-head findings and completed dispositions.\n- **R10.** [Integration Review and Validation](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-06-1641-integration-review/review.md) — criterion evidence, tests, preservation, fresh readers, authorized follow-ups and limits.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T08:44:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T10:49:45Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"743d6a91828e7d141030c152a5885062ed8141b4","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"m2ux:i17/e01/workspace","ref":"i17/e01/workspace","repo":{"id":1137318642,"node_id":"R_kgDOQ8oa8g","name":"workf